cudacapture loader fixtures.

Every .ptx, .sass and .cubin.hex here is byte-exact toolchain output, produced
by gen.sh from the .cu and .cuh sources beside it. Do not edit the generated
files: a fixture adjusted to agree with the loader tests nothing. To change
what a fixture covers, change the source and regenerate.

	CUDA=/usr/local/cuda-13.4 ./gen.sh

Generated 2026-09-22 on gpu-host, an NVIDIA GB10 host, with CUDA 13.4 --
nvcc V13.4.59, nvdisasm V13.4.49, NVVM 7.0.1, PTX ISA 9.4. Target sm_90, which
is not this host's architecture: nothing here is run, so the target is chosen
for a widely available ISA rather than for the machine that built it. gen.sh
builds in /tmp/cudacapture-fixtures so that the absolute path NVVM embeds in
.file is reproducible on any host.

No GPU was used. nvcc, ptxas and nvdisasm compile and disassemble; none of
them touches a device, and nothing here qualifies any claim about GPU
behaviour.

The CUBINs are stored hex-encoded, as the other CUBIN fixtures in this tree
are, so that the repository holds no binary files; the tests decode them on
read.

The three units
---------------

kernels.*   Two entry points with different linkage. scale is a C++ symbol and
            reaches the CUBIN mangled as _Z5scalePfPKff; fill is extern "C" and
            reaches it verbatim. LoadCode joins the CUBIN section, the PTX
            entry and the SASS function on that symbol, so a unit that spells
            every kernel the same way on both sides never exercises the join.
            nvcc also supplies an ambiguity this package needs and cannot
            fabricate honestly: the three parameter loads of scale all sit on
            the declaration line, so that source line identifies no single PTX
            instruction and the PTX tier must report it unknown.

main.*      One translation unit compiled from two files: main.cu includes
            impl.cu, which defines _Z10accumulatePfPKfi at impl.cu:11, a line
            main.cu does not have. A reader that reports the unit's primary
            file with the kernel's line names a location that does not exist.

inline.*    A kernel that force-inlines a device function from helpers.cuh, so
            the disassembler attributes part of the kernel to a header the
            capture does not bundle and carries the call site in an inline
            chain. Those lines are unknowable rather than unclaimed.

The tests that perturb a fixture -- a shifted PTX line table, a stray source
directive, a CRLF disassembly -- transform the generated file in the test
rather than shipping a second, hand-written one. A PTX nobody compiled differs
from the fixture in its header, its registers and its instruction text as well
as in the line table under test, so a loader that refused it would not have
shown that it read the line table at all.

code_template_test.go is the exception in this package: it builds its
artifacts in Go, because a template instantiation's symbol is chosen by the
instantiation and the test varies it.
